{
  "_comment": [
    "Every third-party binary this application bundles, per platform, pinned by SHA-256.",
    "",
    "Upstream ships Windows binaries from a 'Win_Binaries' release tag with no version",
    "numbers, no upstream URLs and no checksums, so a user cannot tell what is inside",
    "the app. This fork fetches each tool from its own official project and refuses to",
    "build if a download does not match the hash recorded here.",
    "",
    "Platform keys are <os>-<machine>: windows-x86_64, linux-x86_64, linux-aarch64,",
    "macos-x86_64, macos-aarch64. fetch_deps.py picks the ones matching the host, or",
    "whatever --platform names.",
    "",
    "Not every tool is available as an official prebuilt binary on every platform.",
    "Artifex publishes no Linux or macOS Ghostscript binaries at all, and pngquant and",
    "jpegoptim publish none either. On those platforms the app falls back to whatever is",
    "on PATH (see find_executable in src/utils.py), so install them with the system",
    "package manager -- README.md has the one-liners. Ghostscript is the only one that",
    "is genuinely required.",
    "",
    "A null sha256 means 'not pinned yet'. Run:  python tools/fetch_deps.py --update-lock",
    "(add --pin-only --platform all to pin every platform from one machine), check the",
    "hashes against the publishers, then commit. CI runs without --update-lock, so an",
    "unpinned or changed dependency fails the build."
  ],
